      "narrative": null,
      "content": "WHO/GPA/TCO/HCS/95.15\n\nPREFACE\n\nIn 1990 WHO published WHO AIDS Series No. 8 Guidelines for counselling about\nHIV infection and disease. This booklet summarized the then current understanding of the\nsubject, including the nature, role, and principles of counselling, psychosocial repercussions\nof HIV infection and associated conditions, and special situations in which counselling is\ncalled for.\n\nHowever, during the past five years, our understanding of the psychosocial impact of\nthe epidemic has progressed and recommended approaches to implementing counselling\nshould be accordingly modified. For",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The preface to 'Counselling for HIV/AIDS: a key to caring', recalling WHO's 1990 counselling guidelines in the AIDS series and explaining how understanding of counselling has developed since. It describes counselling as listening and talking with people about how HIV/AIDS affects them, in many settings.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
