      "pageStart": 8,
      "pageEnd": 8,
      "target": "../sections/page-008.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Counselling for HIV/AIDS: A key to caring\n\n- Carefully devised policies establishing who qualifies to be an HIV/AIDS\ncounsellor are required.\n\n- Within most health and social services, HIV/AIDS counselling is a relatively\nnew activity and, as such, may meet with different reactions from staff and\nsupervisors. In order to avoid serious negative reactions, policy guidance and\napproval is needed as to the role and scope of this activity.\n\nThe guidelines are presented in three parts:\nPart One: HIV/AIDS counselling\n\nThe aim of this section is to describe the essential features of the HIV/AIDS\ncouns",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Lists policy issues the guidelines address, such as defining who qualifies as a counsellor and preparing staff for a new activity. It outlines the document's structure and refers to related WHO/GPA publications.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
