      "target": "../sections/page-009.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "WHO/GPA/TCO/HCS/95.15\n\nPART ONE: HIV/AIDS COUNSELLING\nWhat.is HIV/AIDS counselling?\n\nThe Global Programme on AIDS (GPA) defines HIV/AIDS counselling as “a\nconfidential dialogue between a client and a care provider aimed at enabling the client to cope\nwith stress and take personal decisions related to HIV/AIDS. The counselling process\nincludes an evaluation of personal risk of HIV transmission and facilitation of preventive\n\nak\n\nbehaviour’.\n\nGPA recommends that HIV/AIDS counselling services be established to meet the\nneeds of individuals and families who may have HIV-related or AIDS-related pro",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Opens Part One by giving the Global Programme on AIDS definition of HIV/AIDS counselling as a confidential dialogue that helps clients cope with stress and make personal decisions. It describes the components, including personal risk assessment and planning to reduce risk.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
