      "pageEnd": 12,
      "target": "../sections/page-012.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Counselling for HIV/AIDS: A key to caring\n\nsay, he decided that it would be best if he brought his wife to the next counselling session and\nthat the care-provider would be available to help him to break the news.\n\nBefore he left her office that day, she asked him to describe how his wife might react;\nthen they did some role-plays in which the care-provider played the role of his wife as he\nrehearsed how he would break the news. Eventually he gained confidence that with the help of\nthe counsellor he would be able to find the best way to tell his wife.\n\nBecause of the preparations that he and th",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Continues the case story, describing how the man learned his positive result and was helped through role-play to tell his wife. Over the following years he and his wife received ongoing supportive counselling and social support.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
