      "target": "../sections/page-013.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "WHO/GPA/TCO/HCS/95.15\n\nwork together in confronting the many challenges of AIDS. Whenever he was most sick, a team\nof care-providers visited him regularly at his home, and one member of the team played a major\nrole in supporting him emotionally during the most difficult times. Eventually he became very\nill and was taken to hospital, where a hospital-based religious worker took over some of the role\nof providing emotional support to him and his family. Throughout this period, his colleagues at\nwork and members of a local voluntary organization met many of his material needs.\n\nThe client’s story",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Continues the case story with home-based care, emotional support from care teams, hospital care and spiritual support. It describes how the man told colleagues about his status and educated them about HIV, changing their attitudes.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
