      "target": "../sections/page-014.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Counselling for HIV/AIDS: A key to caring\n\nhis co-workers and this, in turn, meant that his colleagues were available to\nprovide him with social support at critical times during his illness.\n\nAt his home, a social worker on the home-based care team provided him and\nhis wife with ongoing supportive counselling that helped them to cope with the\nmany crises that had arisen during his long illness.\n\nAt the hospital, religious workers not only attended to his spiritual needs but\nalso helped him to make practical preparations relating to the material and\nspiritual needs of is wife and children after",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Concludes the case story with workplace social support and home-based counselling for the couple. It then begins describing the components of counselling, including information on reducing HIV risk through abstinence, fidelity and condoms.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
