      "content": "Counselling for HIV/AIDS: A key to caring\n\n- written procedures for the provision and organization of HIV/AIDS\ncounselling services. The presence of standard procedures will facilitate\nsupervision and monitoring by making it clear what is expected of the staff of\na counselling service. They will enable other staff to know when and where to\nrefer clients who need counselling. Clear procedures on how HIV-related\nclient information is handled will enable high standards of confidentiality to be\nmaintained while at the same time allowing information to flow. In the long\nrun, when staff know what to",
