      "content": "Counselling for HIV/AIDS: A key to caring\n\nis the essential feature of effective counselling, will take place between the\ncare-provider and the client.\n\n(4) Haemophilia will present special problems. Mothers may feel guilty because\nthey have not only passed on the haemophilia but, im many cases, have\nunknowingly injected a contaminated product. When the haemophiliac\nadolescent has been infected as a young child, the parents have to decide how,\nwhen and who will inform the child of this fact. Parents often postpone this\nuntil puberty when they say, “sex may come onto the scene”, Box 6 illustrat",
