      "target": "../sections/page-037.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "WHO/GPA/TCO/HCS/95.15\n\nPeter:\n\nPeter:\n\nMrs J.:\n\nMr J:\n\nPeter:\n\nPeter:\n\nPeter:\n\nPeter:\n\nPeter:\n\nCounsellor:\n\nCounsellor:\n\nCounsellor:\n\nCounsellor:\nCounsellor:\n\nCounsellor:\n\nCounsellor:\n\nCounsellor:\n\nCounsellor:\n\nCounsellor:\n\nPeter, I wonder who you think might worry most about this, you, your father,\nmother, your grandparents or your brother?\n\nI don’t worry about it. My mother does and so does granny. She only wants\nme and my brother to have kids.\n\nSo, Peter, you think that your granny puts pressure on your mother?\n\nShe is always worrying about those things.\n\nMrs J., did you know that Peter thi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Continues the example dialogue in which a counsellor explores worries within a family of an adolescent with haemophilia and HIV. The dialogue is drawn from a published text on systematic HIV counselling.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
