    {
      "id": "library/10665-58534/blocks/prose-page-045",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 45",
      "pageStart": 45,
      "pageEnd": 45,
      "target": "../sections/page-045.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "WHO/GPA/TCO/HCS/95.15\n\nStep Five: Presentation to and review of draft policies by senior officials.\n\nThe draft policy statements are then presented to the senior officials under\nwhose “imprimatur” the policies will be disseminated. The policies are\nreviewed by these officials and are either approved or returned for further\ndevelopment or modification.\n\nStep Six: Finalization and dissemination of policies on HIV/AIDS counselling and\nrelated issues.\n\nAfter review and approval, the new policies are widely disseminated. Any\nretraining of HIV/AIDS counsellors that may be necessary to bring their\npr",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the final steps of policy development: review and approval by senior officials, wide dissemination with any retraining and sensitization of staff at counselling sites, and monitoring of implementation. It refers to an example of a national policy statement in Box 6.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
