      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 46",
      "pageStart": 46,
      "pageEnd": 46,
      "target": "../sections/page-046.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Counselling for HIV/AIDS: A key to caring\n\nTechnical materials and guidelines for HIV/AIDS counselling and related areas.\n\nIn order to implement these policies, programme managers will need to develop more\ndetailed technical guidelines on HIV/AIDS counselling, including how to develop and\nevaluate services and how to train counsellors. In addition, guidance is needed on how\ncounselling interacts with other aspects of HIV/AIDS care, prevention and research.\n\nWHO/GPA has prepared a series of materials (see Annex 1) giving guidance on\nspecific issues such as:\n\n- how to establish HIV/AIDS counsell",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Notes that managers need detailed technical guidelines on counselling services and training and lists WHO/GPA materials on topics such as setting up services, training counsellors, blood transfusion services and breast-feeding advice for HIV-positive mothers. It summarises the importance of developing policies through wide consultation.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
