      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 47",
      "pageStart": 47,
      "pageEnd": 47,
      "target": "../sections/page-047.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "WHO/GPA/TCO/HCS/95.15\n\nBox 6. An example of a policy statement on counselling: Kenya\n\nIt is the Ministry of Health Policy that:\n\n- All health workers should be trained to provide counselling services on a\ncontinuous basis.\n\n- Counselling should not be focused on patients alone, but be extended to the\nfamily.\n\n- There should be district plans of action for AIDS counselling.\n- Confidentiality and ethics should be adhered to at all levels of activities.\n\n- The rights of the individual, culture, social fabrics, etc. should be taken into\nconsideration in AIDS counselling.\n\n- Confirmation of HIV inf",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Presents Kenya's 1988 Ministry of Health policy statement on AIDS counselling, covering training of all health workers, family-centred counselling, district plans, confidentiality and protection from dismissal because of HIV status.",
